  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 88f6fa2b89436164b8e97b17d82dc9a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 3 - Commands
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_command
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 0
  title: Commands
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: 'Commands are pre-programmed functions that allow the robot to perform
    specific tasks.


    In programming, a function is a reusable instruction that
    performs an action when called. Commands in the robot system are functions.


    A
    function is executed by writing its name followed by (). For example:


    moveForward()

    collect()

    wait()


    Some
    functions require additional information called parameters. Parameters are written
    inside the parentheses and are used to control how the function behaves.


    Example:


    discard(0)


    In
    this example, discard is the function name, while 0 is the parameter representing
    the inventory slot index to discard.


    Different functions may require different
    types of parameters such as numbers or text depending on their purpose.'
  isImageBig: 0
